  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25599734",
      "title": "Class-based vs Functional Components: A Summary",
      "sourceHash": "c3ccb60b1ed38a5073c63944b2b5b510a20c4835d01bafcbdc59da4d48b6967d",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.09,
          "end": 4.35,
          "en": "Now that's it for this introduction",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.35,
          "end": 7.12,
          "en": "to class-based components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.12,
          "end": 10.13,
          "en": "I showed you that they exist, how they work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.13,
          "end": 12.02,
          "en": "and how you write your own ones,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.02,
          "end": 15.14,
          "en": "how you work with prompts and the render method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.14,
          "end": 18.41,
          "en": "how you work with state, and also how you work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.41,
          "end": 21.83,
          "en": "with these life cycle methods for side effects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.83,
          "end": 25.28,
          "en": "and we also had a look at how you use context.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.28,
          "end": 27.89,
          "en": "You can build your entire application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.89,
          "end": 30.77,
          "en": "with class-based components if you want to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.77,
          "end": 33.02,
          "en": "That is absolutely fine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.02,
          "end": 36,
          "en": "And in the past, as I mentioned, you had to use them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36,
          "end": 37.77,
          "en": "in some cases.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.77,
          "end": 40.29,
          "en": "But in modern React apps, you typically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.29,
          "end": 43.05,
          "en": "stick to functional components instead,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.05,
          "end": 47.17,
          "en": "simply because they are leaner and more flexible,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.17,
          "end": 49.56,
          "en": "as you learned throughout this module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 49.56,
          "end": 53.27,
          "en": "That's why I also started with functional components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 53.27,
          "end": 56.68,
          "en": "in this course now, because the React Echo system",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 56.68,
          "end": 60.6,
          "en": "transitioned to functional components as the main thing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 60.6,
          "end": 63.82,
          "en": "and that's why I focus on functional components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 63.82,
          "end": 64.79,
          "en": "in this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 64.79,
          "end": 68.21000000000001,
          "en": "Also, going forward, for the rest of this course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 68.21000000000001,
          "end": 70.722,
          "en": "functional components will be the focus",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 70.722,
          "end": 73.68,
          "en": "and I will only occasionally show you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 73.68,
          "end": 76.243,
          "en": "how to work with class-based components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 77.55,
          "end": 80.418,
          "en": "Nonetheless, I wanna emphasize that you don't have to use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 80.418,
          "end": 84.80799999999999,
          "en": "functional components, it is fine to use class-based ones",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 84.80799999999999,
          "end": 87.13,
          "en": "if you prefer them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 87.13,
          "end": 90.2,
          "en": "but chances are that you also see the benefits",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 90.2,
          "end": 93.15,
          "en": "of functional components, and therefore it is fine",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 93.15,
          "end": 96.32,
          "en": "to generally ignore class-based components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 96.32,
          "end": 98.718,
          "en": "With one exception, to which I'll come back to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 98.718,
          "end": 101.42,
          "en": "in a couple of minutes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 101.42,
          "end": 104.69,
          "en": "Now if you're not sure which approach to use,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 104.69,
          "end": 107.85,
          "en": "if you're not sure whether you wanna go with class-based",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 107.85,
          "end": 110.95,
          "en": "or functional components, here's a little",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 110.95,
          "end": 114.49000000000001,
          "en": "helper decision tree, if you wanna call it like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 114.49000000000001,
          "end": 118.25999999999999,
          "en": "As a general rule, you should simply prefer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 118.25999999999999,
          "end": 121,
          "en": "functional components and you should instead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 121,
          "end": 125.85,
          "en": "use class-based components if you personally prefer them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 125.85,
          "end": 127.646,
          "en": "so if you disagree, if you like them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 127.646,
          "end": 131.17,
          "en": "of course you can use them, there's nothing wrong with them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 131.17,
          "end": 134.36,
          "en": "If you are working on a project or if you're in a team",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 134.36,
          "end": 138.63,
          "en": "where there are a lot of class-based components being used,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 138.63,
          "end": 141.21,
          "en": "you might not have a choice then and you might be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 141.21,
          "end": 143.7,
          "en": "confusing your colleagues if you start working",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 143.7,
          "end": 146.24,
          "en": "with functional components only,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 146.24,
          "end": 149.45,
          "en": "and you also should use, and you must use,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 149.45,
          "end": 153.93,
          "en": "class-based components if you're building error boundaries.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 153.93,
          "end": 156.02,
          "en": "Now, that's something we haven't learned yet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 156.02,
          "end": 158.45,
          "en": "but that's exactly what we're going to take a look at",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 158.45,
          "end": 160.023,
          "en": "in the next lecture now.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
